CHAPTER VI

ESTABLISHMENT OF UPTD PPA

Article 30

1. In the context of implementing protection for women and children, the Regional Government establishes UPTD PPA (Women and Children Protection) as a service center for the protection of women and children.
2. UPTD PPA as referred to in paragraph (1) consists of elements of regional apparatus that administer affairs of:a. education;
b. youth;
c. social;
d. cooperatives;
e. industry;
f. manpower;
g. trade;
h. population and civil registration;
i. women's empowerment and child protection; j. public peace and order;
k. regional general hospital;
l. health;
3. UPTD PPA as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be stipulated by a Regent Regulation.
4. Provisions regarding organizational structure, duties and functions of UPTD PPA shall be further regulated by a Regent Regulation.

Article 23

1. Services as referred to in Article 21 letter b are organized through activities:

a. complaint services;
b. health services;
c. counseling;
d. spiritual guidance;
e. social services;
f. legal aid and assistance services; and/or
g. repatriation and social reintegration.
2. Services as referred to in paragraph (1) are organized with:

a. fast and appropriate;
b. safe and comfortable;
c. a sense of empathy;
d. non-discrimination;
e. easily accessible;
f. not charged; and
g. guaranteed confidentiality.
3. Services as referred to in paragraph (1) are organized in an integrated manner by P2TP2A.

REGENT OF PURWAKARTA,

Considering:
a. that every citizen has the right to obtain a sense of security and freedom from all forms of Violence;
b. that violence against women and children in the Region tends to increase, therefore the Regional Government and/or community need to play an active role optimally to provide protection, so that women and children are protected and free from violence or threats of violence, torture, or treatment that degrades human dignity and honor;
c. that protection of women and children is a mandatory concurrent affair which is the authority, obligation, and responsibility of the Regional Government, therefore regulation is needed as a basis for implementing comprehensive and integrated protection for women and children;
d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b and letter c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning the Administration of Protection for Women and Children;

